1]Explain indetail about Aggregation and Composition ?

	->In java thier are 2types of relationships:-
		i)is-a relationship
		ii)has-a relationship
	->is-a relationship can be achieved by making use of inheritance
	->has-a relationship can be achieved by making use of aggregation and composition
	->has-relationship is of 2 types:-
		i)loosely coupled has-a relationship
		ii)tightly couples has-a relationship
		
	->In loosely coupled has-a relationship the aggregate object exists
	->In tightly coupled has-a relationship the composite object exists
	 
Aggregate Objects:-
===================
	->Aggregate objects are such objects which can be accessed even though enclosing object is not accessible

Composite Objects:-
===================
	->Composite objects are such objects which are not accessible if the enclosing object is not accessible.



2]Explain indetail about serialization and de-serialization ?

	->Serialization is the mechanism of converting the state of an object into byte stream is called as
	serialization
	->Where as de-serialization is the reverse process,where the byte stream is used to re-create the actual
	java object in memory is called as de-serialization
	->If i dont want to serialize any data then i use transient keyword
	->After serializing the data,if i change the serial version UID then de-serialization will not work
	because the serial version UID is changed,so serial version UID should be same while doing serialization
	and de-serialization


3]Explain indetail about GarbageCollection ?

	->In java garbage means unreferenced objects
	->Garbage collection is the process of reclaiming the runtime unused memory automatically,in other words
	it is a way to destroy the unused objects
	->In java it is performed automatically,so java provides better memory management
	
How GarbageCollection works in java:-
=====================================
	->In java garbage collection is an automatic process
	->Automatic garbage collection is the process of looking at heap area and identifying which objects are in
	use and which objects are not in use
	->An use object or referenced object means some part of the program still maintains a pointer to that object
	->An un-used object or unreferenced object means no longer refered by any part of the program,so the memory
	used by the unreferenced object can be reclaimed
	->Programmer does not need to mark the object explicitly to delete
	->Garbage collection implementation lives in JVM.
	


4]Explain indetail about interface ?

	->An interface is a blueprint of a class
	->An interface can have abstract methods and variables,by default the variables which are declared inside
	the interface are public static final
	->An interface cannot be instantiated,which means we are not able to create the object for the interface
	but we can create the reference for an interface,using this interface reference we can achieve loose
	coupling hence we can achieve polymorphism
	->Inorder to access the members of an interface the class uses implements keyword
	->In the subclass we has to override the abstract methods or it will shows the compile time error
	->If the subclass is providing the implementation for the abstract methods then it is called as
	implementation class
	->A class can implement any number of interfaces and it will not lead to diamond shape problem
	
		->If thier is a relationship between class to class  we use extends keyword
		->If thier is a relationship between interface to interface we use extends keyword
		->If thier is a relationship between class to interface we use implements keyword
	
	->In java we cannot achieve multiple inheritance using classes,but by using interface we can multiple
	inheritance in java
	
	->If a class partially implements an interface,then the class should be declared as abstract class,but by
	using abstract class  we cannot achieve 100% abstraction or pure abstraction because an abstract class can
	have concrete methods,but by using interface we can achieve 100% abstraction or pure abstraction because an
	interface can have only abstract methods till java7,but in java8 interface where enhanced with default and
	static method,in java9 interface where enhanced with private method so abstraction is slightly reduced
	
	->A class can extends a class and also implements the interface at the same time
	
	->An interface can be created without having any variables and methods,such interfaces are called as 
	tagged interface or marker interface or empty interface
	
	->We create empty interface to give meta data to JVM or libraries so that they apply some special behaviour
	on those classes
	
	->for an example: Serializable is an empty interface that tells the JVM that objects can be serialized. 
	
	
